**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A dropped entry file is an import origin of its own, and one entry is decided on its own (001 §H 'A library entry: its `-json` file, dropped onto the Library or Materials window (§B decision table)'; 001 §B 'one table for catalogues, kit snapshots and single dropped files'; the S3.2 brief). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `ImportOrigin` (step 93) gains `DroppedFileOrigin of file : FileName`, documented as an entry file dropped onto the Library or Materials window, held by its leaf name (`FileName.leafName`). (2) `member this.describe : string` on `ImportOrigin` is its honest render (ELEV002): the catalogue's name for `CatalogueImportOrigin` and the file's text for `DroppedFileOrigin`. `ImportDecision.rowName` (step 93) reads it, so a name collision from a dropped file is `<name> — from <file>`, and one from a catalogue stays `<name> — from <catalogue name>`. (3) `ImportDecision.decide` keeps its rules. Its latest-move condition names `CatalogueImportOrigin (c, _)`, so an entry from a dropped file never moves the latest: a version not held is `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. Its doc says so in one line. (4) On `CatalogueImportProxy`, `member this.decideEntry (origin : ImportOrigin) (incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope) : Result<ImportDecision, CatalogueImportError>` holds the per-envelope body of `decideCatalogue` (step 94 (5)): `tryHeldEntry`, then `heldEntriesNamed` for the envelope's kind and name when nothing is held, then `ImportDecision.decide`. `decideCatalogue` calls it for every envelope in row order and keeps its unlisted rows, so one body decides catalogue rows, dropped files (step 104) and S4.2's kit snapshots. No store is read or written beyond that body, and no other member changes. (5) Tests: `ImportDecisionTests` gains `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`. Under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName "Silicon.material-json")`, Silicon's built-in version 2 against its held version 1 is `VersionNotHeld` defaulting to `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. A user material named `Silicon` under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName "lab-silicon.material-json")` against the held Silicon is `NameCollision` whose `rowName` is `Silicon — from lab-silicon.material-json`. `describe` answers `Built-in` for the class's catalogue origin and `lab-silicon.material-json` for that file's. The facts over `decideCatalogue` keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the origin lands, `ImportOrigin` MUST hold `DroppedFileOrigin`, and `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `decideEntry`, which `decideCatalogue` calls for every envelope; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.
